## Step 2: Read the Week's Daily Memories

Read all consolidated daily memory files from the past 7 days:

```bash
for i in 7 6 5 4 3 2 1; do
  d=$(date -v-${i}d '+%Y-%m-%d')
  if ls memory/daily/${d}*.md >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    ls memory/daily/${d}*.md
  else
    echo "MISSING: $d (no daily consolidation — note this gap in the report)"
  fi
done
```

Read each file that exists; explicitly mention any MISSING days in the report rather than silently skipping them. These are the clean daily summaries produced by the nightly lightweight consolidation. **These daily files are the source of truth for what happened in {{USER_NAME}}'s week — Steps 3.5 and 6 both work from the union of them.**

